known woman now i  could be totally wrong here but i don't  think this has any significance at all  if these flashes are happening  chronologically that means this event  happened  after he got back from korea but before  he got on that bus to chicago in episode  1  meaning this was likely some one night  stand that he was using to forget the  pain of leaving gian  we then see him get on that bus to  chicago before we get a few shots of  things we haven't seen yet  one is of him getting baptized one of  letty and atticus hooked up to some sort  of contraption  all we know other than this is that gia  has seen something that will get atticus  killed  saying that if he goes home he'll die  and what was the word he translated  last episode die atticus wants to know  how jiha predicted his death just like  the translation did or at least that's  what the show is leading us to believe  we aren't sure how atticus will die  but in this universe where we know time  machines and spells that create  invulnerability exist  there are still ways he could die and  come back to life the final scene takes  place between gia  mother and the shaman as an interview  with judy garland plays in the  background  talking about how she had to put up with  years of slander  a people who didn't see her true self  it's really analogous to jia's life  experience constantly being called a  monster with only one person  seeing her true self atticus but there  are a few  interesting bits of information we get  here one we learn that atticus will not  die by jia's hands and two  atticus's visions were things she had  never encountered with any of her  previous victims  i'm curious if atticus is the first man  she's seen memories of in the future  since all her previous victims the last  memory would have been of her killing  them  that's when their life would have ended  jihan wants to know if these visions of  atticus are true  will he die and the shaman says there  will be a big price to pay for